  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### 429s after the fleet scales out\n**Guide:** Failure modes: row 6  \u00b7  **Symptom:** API returns 429 only at some times of day.  \u00b7  **Cause:** Fleet scaled out past the size the per-worker cap assumed.  \u00b7  **Fix:** Size caps for the maximum fleet, or use a shared limiter.\n\n**What to watch:** API rejections (rate) appear only when 10 workers run caps sized for 6; caps sized for 10 or a shared limiter keep API req/s at the limit.\n\n| # | Variant | Phase | Length | What changes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | baseline | 6 workers, caps sized for 6 | 60 s | Per-worker rate = limit / 6. Fine while the fleet really is 6. |\n| 2 | broken | peak: 10 workers, caps still sized for 6 | 90 s | Fleet cap = 10 x limit/6 = 1.67x the API limit; demand 1.8x base exceeds the API limit. |\n| 3 | fixed | peak: 10 workers, caps sized for 10 | 90 s | Fleet cap = API limit. Excess demand waits (and some fails fast) in the workers instead of hitting the API. |\n| 4 | fixed | peak: 10 workers, shared limiter | 90 s | No per-worker cap; every call takes a token from the fleet-wide limiter. |\n\nRun it from the [control page](http://localhost:8088). Blue regions mark phases; red markers are crashes and restarts."
   },
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 7
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "state-timeline",
